WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:13.640 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  of all the fighting game series that  normally transition from arcades to  consoles Tekken has long been the most  generous with its extra features and in  recent years the goal of unlocking and  customizing outfits for the game's large  cast has rounded out the most rewarding  objective of all getting good Tekken 7  keeps most of the series traditions  alive and once again delivers the tight  hard-hitting action Tekken is known for  though it stumbles a little online and  fails to teach new players how to fight  it's otherwise a great fighting game  that confidently claims its position  among the best fighting games today  similar to dead or alive in Virtua  Fighter Tekken 7 is a 3d fighting game  and thus plays quite differently than  its side-scrolling cousins  there are Tekken 7 characters that are  more mobile than others but by and large  this is a game of inches a moment of  indecision or a sloppy move against a  more skilled player can lead to a string  of pummeling strikes and a hasty death  courtesy of the game is long combo  strings  the biggest complaint you can lob at  tekken 7 is that it doesn't do a good  job of explaining the intricacies of its  mechanics let alone how you should  approach learning your character of  choice move lists often hover around 100  entries serving a mix of one-off special  attacks and combos there's no tutorial  mode to speak of so the best you can do  is hop into training mode and shift from  one move to the next none of this is to  say that Tekken 7 is too deep which  would be a ridiculous complaint the  depth of its roster and fighting styles  is to your benefit the point is that new  players will have very little help  learning anything beyond the basics once  they jump into battle but if this isn't  your first king of Iron Fist tournament  and you've kept up with Tekken over its  more than 20 year tenure you will find  that tekken 7 delivers the same great  combat you know and love with a hefty  batch of new characters and a few new  mechanics there are notable new super  moves that can be triggered when a  player's health is dangerously low which  is also the right time to unleash a rage  drive attack a powered-up standard combo  the most important new addition however  is the power crush attack attribute  relevant attacks can absorb incoming  hits mid animation allowing you to risk  a little health to increase your chances  of landing a critical blow and this  injects Tekken's otherwise familiar  fights with a renewed element of  surprise  but the most conspicuous addition to  Tekken 7 must be aqua ma the red-haired  bad guy of Street Fighter Fame  the introduction of fireballs and  hurricane kicks might seem like an odd  fit for Tekken but they don't feel  overpowered in light of the fact that  every character exhibits unique  advantages in battle Street Fighter fans  will appreciate how easy it is to fight  as Akuma as many of his traditional  moves and inputs are present and  accounted for  even street fighters meter based  mechanics have been carried over for his  Tekken debut more interestingly akima  plays a pivotal role in the main story  hailed as the final chapter in the  series long running tale of martial arts  papa Heihachi Mishima and his quarreling  family Tekken sevens main story will  delight long-standing Tekken fans the  only major downfall here is the robotic  and stale narrator in the darkness a  fellow reporter visited me and offered  me a ray of hope in the form of an  expose on G corporation his delivery is  too shallow to take seriously and yet  not witty enough to make his deadpan  cadence funny beyond the two to three  hours spent on the main story every  character not present there in gets  their own brief chapter limited to a  short text intro a single fight and a  unique ending cutscene not all are  created equal but there are gems to find  that are purposefully awkward and  light-hearted admirers of the alien  samurai yoshimitsu will for example  appreciate how he's initially humanized  and made vulnerable in his story only to  be subsequently needed and growing by  the object of his affection as such  Tekken 7 has no trouble living up to the  series reputation for tongue-in-cheek  shenanigans and generously gives you  access to the series entire back  catalogue of cutscenes from the very  first Tekken's low-res cutscenes all the  way to background clips made  specifically for Japanese pachinko  machines there's a lot of tech in  history to unlock and browsing the  collection is a wonderful trip down  memory lane what did you just say you  heard me I said this who talks you  expect us to eat this style you mean it  sucks this pepper beef is too damn spice  okay using fight money earned by playing  the games various modes you can purchase  both these cutscenes but also cosmetic  items for characters these include neon  butterfly wings  a floating clownfish companion and  automatic rifles to name a few  well you certainly don't need to dress  up fighters and ridiculous outfits doing  so will give you a new appreciation for  how comfortable Tekken 7 is in its own  skin  on the one hand it's a hardcore and  demanding fighting game but it's also  happy to be the butt of its own jokes  additional items can also be unlocked  rather than purchased within the  treasure battle mode which puts you in a  series of fights with increasing rewards  and challenges there is a training mode  and in arcade mode where you can  practice your moves  but treasure battle is easily the most  attractive way to spend your off time in  Tekken 7 after all if you're going to  practice your moves before hopping  online to fight you might as well have  something cool to show for it presently  a few days after launch Tekken sevens  online modes are experiencing a few  issues across all platforms and while  these are mostly isolated to ranked  matches it's not uncommon to lose  connections and casual matches either  it's an issue that Bandai Namco is aware  of and plans to fix but at the moment  it's not always easy to get into a match  unless you're willing to hammer attempts  for minutes on it notwithstanding that  online play is currently a crapshoot  Tekken 7 remains an easy game to  recommend its diverse roster is packed  with a wide range of personalities and  fighting styles bolstered by a raucous  attitude that begs to be taken seriously  while simultaneously mocking its more  peculiar whims in the process Tekken  fans will find their next favorite  fighting game one that's a product of  decades worth of refinement and while  some of this depth will be lost or out  of reach for newcomers there's enough  fun to be had outside of hardcore  competition to keep players from all  walks of gaming thoroughly entertained  [Music]  you  [Music]

